WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.200
Fantasy Premier League hands you 100 million pounds and asks for fifteen players.

00:06.200 --> 00:13.175
After five gameweeks of the 2026 to 27 season, the data already shows where the points are hiding.

00:13.175 --> 00:15.450
Here is the three minute version.

00:16.150 --> 00:17.875
First, the rules.

00:17.875 --> 00:28.100
100 million pounds buys fifteen players: two goalkeepers, five defenders, five midfielders and three forwards, with at most three from any one club.

00:28.100 --> 00:31.100
Every decision is bounded by that budget.

00:31.800 --> 00:33.500
Now the surprise.

00:33.500 --> 00:36.750
Five of the fifteen highest scorers are defenders.

00:36.750 --> 00:44.250
Jayden Bogle of Leeds has 42 points at 4.6 million pounds, which is 9.1 points per million.

00:44.250 --> 00:49.275
Pascal Gross returns 8.1, and Maxim De Cuyper 7.6.

00:49.275 --> 00:54.175
Erling Haaland, at 15.6 million, returns just 2.5.

00:54.875 --> 00:58.050
Clean sheets belong to teams, not players.

00:58.050 --> 01:04.425
Brighton have the best goal difference in the league, plus 11, and supply two of the leading defenders.

01:04.425 --> 01:08.225
Manchester City are plus 8 and supply Gvardiol.

01:08.225 --> 01:13.850
So buy the cheapest starting defender from the best current defence, not the most famous name.

01:14.550 --> 01:16.850
Goalkeepers are even flatter.

01:16.850 --> 01:21.900
Tzolakis of Hull City has 34 points at 4.7 million.

01:21.900 --> 01:28.600
Raya of Arsenal has 30 at 6.1, and Alisson of Liverpool 27 at 5.5.

01:28.600 --> 01:33.875
Hull face more shots, so Tzolakis has made 17 saves to Raya's 9.

01:33.875 --> 01:37.000
Spend the minimum that buys a guaranteed starter.

01:37.700 --> 01:39.750
Be careful with hot starts.

01:39.750 --> 01:47.550
Expected goal involvement, or X G I, is expected goals plus expected assists, and it predicts better than points.

01:47.550 --> 01:52.675
Pascal Gross has 7 goal involvements from just 2.63 expected.

01:52.675 --> 01:55.825
Joao Pedro has 6 from 2.36.

01:55.825 --> 01:59.500
Igor Thiago has only 1 from 3.29.

01:59.500 --> 02:03.000
Sell the overperformers and buy the underperformers.

02:03.700 --> 02:06.850
Ownership records the past, not the present.

02:06.850 --> 02:12.400
Szoboszlai is owned by 32.9 percent of managers but has a form of 3.0.

02:12.400 --> 02:16.825
Bogle is owned by just 7.1 percent, with a form of 9.0.

02:16.825 --> 02:27.225
And prices follow transfers: Gross rose 0.1 million after 765,270 net transfers in, so buy early.

02:27.925 --> 02:29.775
Finally, look ahead.

02:29.775 --> 02:33.600
Every match carries a difficulty rating from 1 to 5.

02:33.600 --> 02:38.025
Over gameweeks 6 to 8, Fulham average 2.0 while Leeds average 4.0.

02:38.025 --> 02:42.425
Form is only worth buying when the next three games let it continue.

02:43.125 --> 02:54.550
So: spend on cheap defenders from strong defences, keep goalkeepers cheap, trust expected goal involvement over hot streaks, follow the fixtures, and buy before the price rises.

02:54.550 --> 03:00.425
Every number here can be rechecked from the F P L A P I, or the archived data on GitHub.

03:00.425 --> 03:02.150
Thanks for watching.
